SUMMARY:✨ 7-DAY Norway Fjords & Outdoor Adventures Cruise (2026) 🌊❄
 ️
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n**A Onc
 e-in-a-Lifetime Journey — Luxury\, Adventure\, and Pure Nordic Magic!**\
 n\nThey’re about **where you breathe differently**\, where time slows\, 
 and where you remember what it feels like to feel *alive*.\nThis is one of
  those journeys.\n\nFrom **Sunday\, July 26 to Sunday\, August 2\, 2026**\
 , a small\, thoughtfully curated group of travelers will sail through Norw
 ay’s most breathtaking fjords aboard **Holland America’s flagship\, MS
  Rotterdam** — one of the most elegant and quietly luxurious ships at se
 a.\n\nThis experience is designed specifically for **solo travelers and in
 dependent spirits** who want:\n\n• real connection (without forced socia
 lizing)\n• nature\, walking\, hiking\, and outdoor beauty\n• exception
 al food and thoughtful service\n• comfort\, calm\, and meaningful shared
  moments\n• and the ease of travelling with a group — without feeling 
 like part of a tour bus\n\nThis is **not** a party cruise.\n\nIt’s a jou
 rney for people who love conversation\, fresh air\, and waking up somewher
 e extraordinary.\n\n**A Curated Small-Group Journey for Curious\, Connecti
 on-Seeking Travelers**\n\nHave you ever dreamed of gliding through misty f
 jords surrounded by cascading waterfalls\, emerald cliffs\, and tiny Vikin
 g villages perched at the edge of the world? 🌄🐋 This **is your momen
 t** — the ultimate *bucket list* experience you’ll remember forever.\n
 \nThis is *not* just another vacation — it’s an *adventure through the
  heart of Norway*. You’ll experience majestic fjords\, glaciers\, Viking
  farms\, and picture-perfect ports like **Haugesund\, Molde\, Olden\, and 
 Sandnes (Stavanger)**. Whether you’re hiking up to **Pulpit Rock**\, cru
 ising past glacier-fed waterfalls\, or sipping coffee on your private balc
 ony\, every moment will feel like something out of a dream. 💫\n[Click H
 ere To See The Crusie We Are Going On!](https://www.hollandamerica.com/en/
 ca/find-a-cruise/e6n07i/y651)\n\n## 🛳️ Why This Cruise Is Different\n
 \nWe’ll be sailing aboard the **MS Rotterdam**\, Holland America Line’
 s newest flagship — a ship known for:\n✨ refined design and spacious p
 ublic areas\n✨ outstanding live music and entertainment\n✨ world-class
  dining (with real ingredients and real flavour)\n✨ an adult\, relaxed\,
  and international crowd\n✨ service that feels attentive\, not intrusive
 \nYou’ll never feel rushed.\nYou’ll never feel lost.\n\n***\n\n## 🏔
 ️ The Experience: Norway at Its Most Beautiful\n\nNorway is one of those
  places that photos never quite capture.\nYou feel it instead.\n\nOur rout
 e includes:\n• **Haugesund** – Viking history\, coastal walks\, and qu
 iet charm\n• **Molde** – panoramic mountain views and forest paths\n
 • **Olden** – glaciers\, waterfalls\, and the unforgettable Loen Skyli
 ft\n• **Sandnes / Stavanger** – gateway to **Pulpit Rock (Preikestolen
 )**\, one of the most iconic hikes in the world\n\nBetween ports\, we’ll
  enjoy **scenic cruising inside the fjords** — towering cliffs\, waterfa
 lls spilling straight into the sea\, and long summer days that seem to str
 etch forever. 🌿💧\n\nThis is a trip for people who like to:\n• walk
 \, explore\, and be outside\n• take photos — then put the camera away\
 n• share a meal and a story at the end of the day\n\n## 🤍 Hosted with
  Care (This Matters)\n\nYour host\, **Mathew Mac Lean**\, previously worke
 d for **Holland America Line** and has sailed in Norway multiple times.\nT
 hat means:\n• insider knowledge of the ship and how to use it well\n• 
 guidance on which excursions are worth it (and which aren’t)\n• though
 tful group coordination — without micromanaging\n• a calm\, welcoming 
 presence focused on community and comfort\nThis trip is intentionally limi
 ted to **approximately 12 guests**.\nSmall enough to feel personal.\nLarge
  enough to feel social.\n\n***\n\n## 🍽️ Food\, Comfort & the “Have 
 It All” Experience\n\nAll cabins include Holland America’s **Have It A
 ll Package**\, which means:\n🥂 drinks (alcoholic & non-alcoholic)\n📶
  premium Wi-Fi\n🍽️ one specialty dining experience\n☕ specialty cof
 fees & teas\n🚶‍♂️ $100 shore excursion credit\nDining is flexible
  — shared meals if you want them\, quiet dinners if you don’t.\nThere 
 is **no pressure to socialize**\, just opportunity.\n\n***\n\n## 💰 Inve
 stment (and Why It’s Worth It)\n\nThis is a premium experience — desig
 ned to be smooth\, beautiful\, and deeply memorable.\n\nAll prices in CAD\
 , solo occupancy:\n• **Inside Cabin** – $4\,423\n• **Ocean View** 
 – $5\,450\n• **Verandah (Balcony)** – $5\,807\n\n💳 Deposit to res
 erve your cabin: **approximately $520**\n(Prices will rise as availability
  decreases.)\n\nPrefer to share a cabin?\nYou can reduce the total cost by
  about **$1\,000 per person**.\n\n***\n\n## 🧭 Who This Trip Is For\n\nT
 his journey is ideal for you if:\n• you enjoy traveling solo but not fee
 ling alone\n• you prefer connection over crowds\n• you love nature\, s
 cenery\, and gentle adventure\n• you appreciate good food and thoughtful
  spaces\n• you’re independent\, curious\, and open-hearted\n\nThis tri
 p may **not** be for you if:\n• you’re looking for nightlife or partyi
 ng\n• you want a rigid\, highly scheduled tour\n• you need constant st
 imulation\nAnd that’s okay — this trip knows exactly what it is.\n\n**
 *\n\n## 🌟 What Happens Next\n\nIf this speaks to you — even a little 
 — your next step is simple:\n\n👉 **[Join the online information sessi
 on](https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/31276848
 8/?slug=toronto-movies-and-social-group&eventId=311966342&isFirstPublish=t
 rue)**\n\nAsk questions.\nMeet others who are curious.\nGet a feel for the
  group and the journey.\nThere’s no pressure — just clarity.\nBecause 
 the truth is:\nThe hardest part of a trip like this…\nis giving yourself
  permission to go.\n\n* [Click Here To Watch The Info Video!](https://www.
 youtube.com/watch?v=z0QcTyDmiT0)\n\n***\n\n### 🗓️ Itinerary Highlight
 s\n\n* **Day 1:** Rotterdam\, Netherlands\n* **Day 2:** Sea Day (relax\, e
 xplore\, unwind)\n* **Day 3:** Haugesund 🇳🇴\n* **Day 4:** Molde (wit
 h scenic fjord cruising!)\n* **Day 5:** Olden (glaciers + outdoor adventur
 es)\n* **Day 6:** Sandnes (Stavanger – Pulpit Rock\, Viking charm)\n* **
 Day 7:** Sea Day\n* **Day 8:** Return to Rotterdam\n\n***\n\n### 🧭 Logi
 stics & Extras\n\n* ✈️ **Flights:** Arrive in Amsterdam a day early (i
 t’s cheaper & safer — you don’t want to miss the ship!)\n* 🏨 **Ho
 tel:** We’ll coordinate affordable group options.\n* 🚶‍♂️ **Exc
 ursions:** Budget around $500 — Norway is expensive but *beyond worth it
 .*\n* 💆‍♀️ **Optional extras:** Spa\, specialty coffees\, bingo\,
  etc.\n* 🧳 **Insurance:** Both travel & health insurance are *strongly 
 recommended.*\n\n### Excursions\n\n## 🛡️ **JULY 28 — HAUGESUND**\n\
 n## ⭐ *Viking Kings & Coastal Beauty*\n\nWe’ll explore the birthplace 
 of Norway and visit the **Avaldsnes Viking Village** — longhouses\, cost
 umed Vikings\, coastal views\, and real immersive history.\n**Why it’s g
 reat:**\n\n* Authentic Viking experience\n* Beautiful\, walkable harbour t
 own\n* Scenic coastal paths\n\n***\n\n## 🌄 **JULY 29 — MOLDE**\n\n###
  ⭐ *Panoramic Peaks & Fjord Walks*\n\nA relaxing nature day! We’ll vis
 it **Varden Viewpoint**\, famous for its 200+ mountain panorama\, then enj
 oy the gentle trails of **Moldemarka**.\n**Why it’s great:**\n\n* Quiet 
 and scenic\n* Incredible mountain views\n* Easy forest walking paths\n\n**
 *\n\n## 🚡 **JULY 30 — OLDEN**\n\n### ⭐ *Loen Skylift — Fjord to M
 ountain Top*\n\nRide the **Loen Skylift** straight up to unforgettable fjo
 rd views\, alpine trails\, and a cozy mountaintop café.\n**Why it’s gre
 at:**\n\n* One of Norway’s most beautiful fjords\n* Huge scenery in a ti
 ny town\n* Walk\, explore\, relax on the mountain\n\n## ⛰️ **JULY 31 
 — STAVANGER / SANDNES**\n\n### ⭐ *Pulpit Rock — Norway’s Most Famo
 us Hike*\n\nThis is the big one — and for timing and convenience\, **we
 ’ll be doing this hike through the cruise line**. It ensures a smooth\, 
 stress-free experience with guaranteed return to the ship.\nWe’ll make o
 ur way to **Pulpit Rock (Preikestolen)**\, the legendary cliff towering 60
 0 metres above the Lysefjord — one of the world’s most photographed vi
 ewpoints.\n**Why it’s great:**\n\n* The most iconic view in all of Norwa
 y\n* A doable\, rewarding 3–4 hour hike\n* Breathtaking scenery from sta
 rt to finish\n* After the hike\, there’s still free time to explore Stav
 anger’s charming old town\n\n***\n\n### 🧠 How It Works\n\n* You’ll 
 book through our **official Holland America cruise consultant** (details p
 rovided after signup).\n* Mathew will handle all the *fun stuff* — dinin
 g plans\, group excursions\, and onboard activities.\n* Once your deposit 
 is confirmed\, you’ll move from “Interested” to “Going.”\n\n***\
 n\n### 🚫 Important Notes\n\n* This is an **adult-only (21+)** cruise.\n
 * Prices will increase as the sailing date approaches — **lock in early!
 **\n* Members must be independent and self-sufficient during travel.\n\n**
 *\n\n### 🎥 Watch the Cruise Preview\n\n📺 *[Click here to see what yo
 ur adventure will look like!](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qd7blqrRJSM)
 *\n(*Note: video may show slightly different ports.*)\n\n***\n\n### 💌 Q
 uestions?\n\nEmail **Mathew Mac Lean** at **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\no
 r post in the comments below.
